%  16 selections translated to abcs from notation mostly presented in Silver Apple News #9 (2004)
%  more tunes related to recordings promoted in Silver Apple 9 found in another abc file located at
%  http://www.cranfordpub.com/tunes/abcs/SAN9.abc
%  most of the source CDs are available from cranfordpub.com
%  hard copy of current Silver Apple News can be requested from
%  Cranford Publications -  http://www.cranfordpub.com

% selecions chosen both to promote artists recordings and because they are not found
% in books or abcs currently published by Cranford Publications
% rather than duplicate, some tunes which were first published in Silver Apple 9 aren't here
% instead they can be found in other abcs that have been posted alongside of the source CD
%  some of the settings below are intentionally not literal transcriptions
% instead they have been consciously simplified to create concise memorable arrangements
% If anyone know has further information or concerns about any of theses tunes or settings
% please contact psc@cranfordpub.com so it can be updated or removed

% like our print books, this file is sorted alphabetically by key /mode /tune type

% NOTE -  metronome settings are arbitrary and may be adjusted using the Q field

% composers and their heirs retain performance, print and mechanical copyrights
% for composer/ copyright contact info (for licencing etc.) email info@cranfordpub.com

% NOTE
% Although an abc program installed in your computer has more functionality,
% a browser can now convert a properly formatted abc tune to on-screen music.
% Like the 'Hotmail concept', this enables translation of abc tunes from anyone's computer.
% Just 'copy' an individual tune from the text file below
% Then paste contents of your clipboard into on-line form. Submit and presto!!
% for instructions go to http://www.cranfordpub.com
% look for the link <Convert ABCs>


