X:16
T:Mike MacDougall's
T:Traditional Jig
R:jig
O:20st century Cape Breton
S:Silver Apple News, 2004
D:Wendy MacIsaac, Timeline
H:I played this tune for Johnny Wilmot in about 1980. Since Johnny didn't know it, he assumed it was a new tune I had written. I had heard it from Mike MafcDouglal hence the title. Now a popular tune, Wendy recorded it as Traditional Jig. Mike died in 1982 and the composer remains anonymous.
Z:Paul Stewart Cranford (P.S.C.), <http://www.cranfordpub.com>
